    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0092" n="10" xml:id="pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d12-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Excerpts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-22">22 October
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Roosevelt
                    Personal and Top Secret Number 801.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Para 8. I was delighted to hear from U. J. that you had suggested a triple
                    meeting towards the end of November at a Black Sea port. I think this a very
                    fine idea, and hope you will let me know about it in due course. I will come
                    anywhere you two desire.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d12-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d12-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels. For other
                    excerpts from this telegram, see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg159">pp. 159</ref>–<ref target="#pg160">160</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg206">206</ref>, <ref target="#pg328">328</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg400">400</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
